12166	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s9","entry":{"id":"review-d2e10dc698b5865c044835926c86a022","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T10:58:17.042Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The design supplies the complete per-site replacement and verification mapping required by s9 ac6.","evidence":"DEF §6.9 requires 'every site has an entry in the replacement table, a test that runs through the registry with a recorded executor'. The LLD describes a future table but supplies no rows; identity API calls, stamp helpers, and the team operation mappings remain unspecified. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, src/understanding/identity.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/range-base.ts, src/workflow/team/policy-refresh.ts]","action":"Include the replacement table in the design, with exact tool inputs, execution context, result adaptation and a recorded-executor test for every site.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"resolveStoryRangeBase returns an invalid result for a stored base whose commit no longer exists.","evidence":"readBuildStart returns { kind: 'invalid', reason: 'rangeBase names a commit this repository does not have' }. resolveStoryRangeBase instead logs 'ignoring an invalid build-start file' and continues through upstream stamps and introducing commits, ultimately returning string | undefined. Upstream stampedBase values are not checked for commit existence. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/range-base.ts]","action":"Correct the edge case and preserve the distinction between stamp validation and range resolution, including fallback precedence.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"mergeInProgress distinguishes exit 1 from other failures before checking SQUASH_MSG.","evidence":"The complete function returns true on successful MERGE_HEAD verification, logs and returns false when status !== 1, and otherwise resolves --git-path SQUASH_MSG and checks existsSync. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/story-commits.ts]","action":"Preserve this distinction explicitly in the facade adaptation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"callTool provides the stated definition-provenance check and typed result wrapper.","evidence":"callTool checks getTool(tool.id) and isDefinitionOf(registered, tool), rejects missing or different definitions, awaits executeTool, and returns checked data or a ToolFailure. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts]","action":"Reuse this helper without duplicating its provenance or output checking.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The existing gh_auth status operation can support the specified identity-command replacement.","evidence":"gh_auth status runs ['auth', 'status'] with only an optional hostname, limitS: 30, and converts text through ghConvert into { hosts: [...] }. githubIdentities requires '--json hosts', preserves spawn/truncation distinctions, and additionally calls 'gh api --hostname ... users/<login>' to obtain node_id. Replacing its command seam with an auth-status-only function cannot preserve these operations. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/account.ts, src/understanding/identity.ts, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Resolve the s5 dependency before approval: specify exact tools and adapters for both JSON status and per-host user lookup, retaining budgets and node_id semantics.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The seven listed resolveStoryRangeBase callers and described leaf migration cover its async ripple.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts also calls '(deps.resolveRangeBase ?? resolveStoryRangeBase)(repoPath, epicHash, storyId)' and immediately consumes the base. Within range-base.ts, readBuildStart calls commitExists and stampBuildStart calls both readBuildStart and headFullSha; implement.ts consumes stampBuildStart synchronously. These contracts are absent from the enumerated reshaping. [files: src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/range-base.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/phases/implement.ts]","action":"Add resolveCodeReviewSubject and its dependency seam, readBuildStart, stampBuildStart and their callers/tests to the explicit async migration inventory. The analyzer returned incomplete graph coverage, so reconcile it with source searches.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The corpus BinaryGitRunner replacement is specified sufficiently to preserve its byte contract.","evidence":"readPinnedSources calls only ['cat-file', '--batch'] and passes the returned framed bytes to decodeObject. git_cat_file instead returns parsed objects with contentBase64 and defaults maxBytes to 4 MiB. The LLD specifies neither reconstruction of the expected frame nor maxBytes selection, and incorrectly leaves the actual command inventory unknown. [files: src/design/corpus/sources/git-reader.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/cat-file.ts]","action":"Document the exact one-command adapter, frame reconstruction or deliberate reader-interface change, maxBytes and aggregate budgets, and error-code mapping. Retain identity/hash validation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Persisted range records can remain unchanged while git access becomes asynchronous.","evidence":"BuildStartStamp stores epicHash, storyId, rangeBase and stampedAt; readBuildStart validates these fields. The resolver also reads meta.rangeBase and legacy body.commit without persisting execution context. Changing the execution mechanism requires no new stored field. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/range-base.ts]","action":"Keep these shapes and fallback order unchanged; include legacy body.commit and upstream-stamp cases in regression coverage.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The existing git_ls_files tool preserves the ignore filter's supported output budget.","evidence":"The old filter uses 'maxBuffer: 50 * 1024 * 1024'. git_ls_files calls readGit without an output-budget override; runShell defaults DEFAULT_MAX_BYTES to 10 * 1024 * 1024. Thus the design's open budget question is a confirmed incompatibility: repositories previously supported can degrade to permissive filtering. [files: src/analyze/context/repo-ignore-filter.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/ls-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Resolve the family-tool budget dependency and specify the supported limit before migration; reconcile §2.9 with the corrected {cached:true, others:true} input.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"s9 can land before s10 while moved team helpers require a daemon-local registry.","evidence":"src/cli/services/team.ts imports refreshPolicy directly and teamRefresh awaits it in the client process; it also directly invokes team gate helpers. The split note makes s10 depend on s9, but the proposed daemon-only facade would make these existing paths return registry failures during that interval. Naming only workflow.ts misses this concrete consumer. [files: src/cli/services/team.ts, src/cli/services/index.ts, src/workflow/team/policy-refresh.ts, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Agree a compatible transition with s10 and document client → daemon ownership and execution flow for team.ts and related services. Prose or a small sequence diagram is sufficient; do not leave the boundary as an unresolved runtime break.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed failure handling matches the executor's cancellation and approval-timeout discriminants.","evidence":"ToolDenialReason is 'declined' | 'timed-out' | 'no-client' | 'cancelled', rather than 'expired'. Executor cancellation before execution produces kind 'denied' with cancellation denial; cancelledFail for running git produces kind 'rejected' and cancellation text. There is no top-level ToolFailure kind 'cancelled'. GitRun also lacks the timedOut property the LLD later promises. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts, src/workflow/team/git.ts, src/workflow/team/git-async.ts]","action":"Use the actual shared union values and define a precise adapter for pre-execution cancellation, in-flight cancellation, timeout and approval timeout. Define a result type that retains the refresh's required timedOut information.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Every failed or aborted refresh call stops further work, consistently with the documented preservation behavior.","evidence":"refreshLocked currently performs anchor lookup after a failed show, may write a sighting before reporting unreadable policy, and treats setRemoteHead failure as a warning on the normal success path. A blanket 'any call failed' stop changes these semantics, while retaining the old flow after cancellation would violate ac3. [files: src/workflow/team/policy-refresh.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"Separate ordinary failure handling from abort/deadline handling per call. Specify where records must still be written, where cosmetic failure remains a warning, and where cancellation stops all subsequent calls.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The proposed tests fully demonstrate ac2 and ac6 rather than only representative helper behavior.","evidence":"DEF ac2 explicitly includes stages that 'converts, hands over or signs off'; its LLD test mapping lists range resolution, story changes, gate stamps and validation only. ac6 requires a recorded-executor test per site, but no such mapping is provided for convert/plan, companion/header, handoff, signoff, identity user lookup or the omitted stamp-chain contracts. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, src/workflow/runners/build/range-base.ts, src/workflow/team/policy-refresh.ts, src/understanding/identity.ts]","action":"Add per-site executor assertions and behavioral cases for conversion, companion headers, handoff/signoff artifacts and records, identity node_id resolution, and build-start stamp retention/rebuild logic. Tie each to the replacement-table row.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":8,"med":2,"low":3,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T10:58:17.042Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
